{{!
    @template local_ai_course_assistant/analytics_tab_bycourse

    By Course tab of the analytics dashboard. Replaces the innerHTML string
    that amd/src/analytics_dashboard.js used to build for this pane
    (CONTRIB-10574 #278). Course names come back from the web service and are
    auto-escaped here instead of being hand-escaped in JavaScript.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * chartheight - pixel height for the bar chart canvas
    * str_course - column heading for the course name
    * str_active - column heading for active AI users
    * str_messages - column heading for the message count
    * str_permsg - column heading for messages per student
    * str_returnrate - column heading for the return rate
    * str_avgsession - column heading for the average session length
    * rows - one entry per course, each with course, active, messages,
      permsg, returnrate and avgsession

    Example context (json):
    {
        "chartheight": 80,
        "str_course": "Course",
        "str_active": "Active AI users",
        "str_messages": "Messages",
        "str_permsg": "Messages per student",
        "str_returnrate": "Return rate",
        "str_avgsession": "Average session",
        "rows": [
            {
                "course": "Introduction to Business",
                "active": "41",
                "messages": "612",
                "permsg": "14.9",
                "returnrate": "38%",
                "avgsession": "7 min"
            }
        ]
    }
}}
<div class="row mb-4">
    <div class="col-12">
        <canvas id="sola-chart-bycourse" height="{{chartheight}}"></canvas>
    </div>
</div>
<table class="table table-sm table-striped sola-analytics-table">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>{{str_course}}</th>
            <th>{{str_active}}</th>
            <th>{{str_messages}}</th>
            <th>{{str_permsg}}</th>
            <th>{{str_returnrate}}</th>
            <th>{{str_avgsession}}</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        {{#rows}}
            <tr>
                <td>{{course}}</td>
                <td>{{active}}</td>
                <td>{{messages}}</td>
                <td>{{permsg}}</td>
                <td>{{returnrate}}</td>
                <td>{{avgsession}}</td>
            </tr>
        {{/rows}}
    </tbody>
</table>
